It builds on work by others, whose licences it keeps:

  * Monty — the Thousand Brains Project's sensorimotor framework
    (https://github.com/thousandbrainsproject/tbp.monty), MIT, Copyright (c)
    Thousand Brains Project. This is a reimplementation of it; the module map in
    `lib/monty/module_map/data.ex` says which modules correspond.
  * ExQuiddity — quiddity and the exact B-rep under it, bound for the BEAM
    (https://github.com/d-led/ex.quiddity), MPL-2.0 for the binding and Apache
    License 2.0 for the engine (https://github.com/pzfreo/quiddity). Used as a
    dependency by the CAD world; not modified here.

The STEP parts under `priv/cad_experiments/parts/` are geometry the CAD
experiments step, copied from the checkouts that draw them so that this
repository runs without another one beside it:

  * `plate.step` and `blend.step` / `blend-big.step` are this project's own
    fixtures, from `ex.monty.cad` and `ex.quiddity` respectively (same licence).
  * `solidcraft-plate.step` is an unmodified STEP export of SolidCraft's own
    sample plate — https://github.com/tangency-labs/solidcraft — MIT OR
    Apache-2.0, Copyright (c) SolidCraft contributors. It is a parametric CAD
    modeller whose examples are JSON models; the part is what
    `solidcraft-cli run <model>.json --out <part>.step` writes. The model is used
    as geometry only: nothing of SolidCraft is linked, copied or modified here.
